<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Newlands Resolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Newlands Resolution was the joint resolution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-congress">United States Congress</a>, introduced by Representative Francis G. Newlands, by which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> annexed the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> in July 1898. A joint resolution was used because an annexation treaty could not win the two-thirds Senate majority required. It passed during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a>, which had shown Hawaii's value as a naval base, and Hawaii became a US territory in 1900.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/newlands-resolution.jpg" alt="Newlands Resolution" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frank Davey · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lowering_the_Hawaiian_flag_at_Annexation_ceremony_(PPWD-8-3-006).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
